{
  "$comment": "Hand-reviewed goldens for the paid client license (docs/spec/license.md). A human decided every `expected` value here; `scripts/gen-license-fixture.mjs` fills in ONLY the two test-only RSA key pairs and the `activation` strings derived from each case's `sign` block, because a signature is not something a reviewer can type. The private keys are test-only and are never used outside this file. Asserted by crates/futo-notes-license/tests/conformance.rs, which is wired into `just test-rust`. Timestamps are RFC 3339 UTC; `now` is the instant the case is evaluated at.",
  "keys": {
    "org": {
      "$comment": "Stands in for the FUTO Notes FUTOpay org key pair.",
      "publicKeySpkiBase64": "",
      "privateKeyPkcs8Base64": ""
    },
    "otherOrg": {
      "$comment": "A different org's key pair \u2014 proves a signature from the wrong signer is rejected rather than merely mis-parsed.",
      "publicKeySpkiBase64": "",
      "privateKeyPkcs8Base64": ""
    }
  },
  "constants": {
    "$comment": "The baked-in constants every shell must agree on. Selection between environments follows the existing dev/prod split (M3).",
    "productSlug": "futo-notes",
    "checkoutProductSlug": "futo-notes-license",
    "orgSlug": "futo-notes",
    "deepLinkScheme": "futonotes",
    "keyAlphabet": "ABCDEFGHJKMNPQRSTUVWXYZ123456789",
    "supportMailto": "mailto:support@futo.tech",
    "buyUrls": {
      "$comment": "The Buy / Renew destination, opened in the system browser. It is the generated checkout on the environment's own pay2 host \u2014 there is no pay.futo.tech landing page and there will not be one (product decision 2026-09-10). Environment-split like the verification key and the activation host (M3), so a .dev build reaches staging checkout. The product segment is the STOREFRONT slug, `futo-notes-license` \u2014 not `futo-notes`, which is the product field inside an activation payload and names nothing in the storefront (its /price answers \"Product not found: futo-notes\", observed 2026-09-10). `platform` is attribution only; `success` is the buyer's return URL and is empty because an app-initiated purchase has none to hand back \u2014 the storefront's own links pass `success=redirect-to-organization-page` instead, a difference we do not adopt.",
      "production": {
        "desktop": "https://pay2.futo.org/checkout/polar/futo-notes/futo-notes-license/checkout-ready?platform=desktop&success=",
        "ios": "https://pay2.futo.org/checkout/polar/futo-notes/futo-notes-license/checkout-ready?platform=ios&success=",
        "android": "https://pay2.futo.org/checkout/polar/futo-notes/futo-notes-license/checkout-ready?platform=android&success="
      },
      "staging": {
        "desktop": "https://staging-pay2.futo.org/checkout/polar/futo-notes/futo-notes-license/checkout-ready?platform=desktop&success=",
        "ios": "https://staging-pay2.futo.org/checkout/polar/futo-notes/futo-notes-license/checkout-ready?platform=ios&success=",
        "android": "https://staging-pay2.futo.org/checkout/polar/futo-notes/futo-notes-license/checkout-ready?platform=android&success="
      }
    },
    "environments": {
      "production": {
        "pay2BaseUrl": "https://pay2.futo.org",
        "bundleIds": [
          "com.futo.notes"
        ]
      },
      "staging": {
        "pay2BaseUrl": "https://staging-pay2.futo.org",
        "bundleIds": [
          "com.futo.notes.dev"
        ]
      },
      "$comment": "Which build talks to which org. The `.dev` id suffix IS the dev/prod split (M3) and is the only selector, because the native shells compile the FFI with `release-ffi` for their dev apps too \u2014 a compile-profile test would put a .dev phone build on the production key."
    }
  },
